# Responsive UI

Every UI component and page must work on **desktop browsers** and **mobile phones**. Design mobile-first, then enhance for larger screens.

## Requirements

- No horizontal overflow on narrow viewports (~320px+).
- Text, buttons, and inputs remain readable and tappable on mobile (min ~44px touch targets for interactive elements).
- Layouts must adapt — never rely on a fixed desktop-only width.
- Images and media scale with `max-w-full`, `object-cover`, or equivalent.
- Tables and wide content need a mobile strategy (stacked cards, horizontal scroll, or `hidden md:table` + mobile alternative).

## Tailwind patterns

Use responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`). Match existing project conventions:

```tsx
// Layout — stack on mobile, columns on desktop
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

// Spacing & typography — scale up on larger screens
<div className="p-4 md:p-10 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
<h1 className="text-3xl md:text-5xl">

// Show/hide by breakpoint when layouts differ
<table className="hidden md:table">...</table>
<div className="md:hidden">...</div>

// Flex — wrap or stack on small screens
<div className="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
```

## Checklist before finishing UI work

- [ ] Renders without broken layout at ~375px width (phone)
- [ ] Renders correctly at ~1280px width (desktop)
- [ ] No clipped or overlapping content at either size
- [ ] Forms and actions usable without zooming on mobile
